# Dependencies are never committed.
node_modules/
*.tgz
*.tsbuildinfo

# `lib/` IS committed, deliberately: this plugin installs from git
# (`dsh plugin --profile web add github:chen8923/dsh-task-progress`), and a
# git-hosted package that has to build needs pnpm's build-script allowlist,
# keyed by the exact commit — which turns a one-line install into a two-step
# one whose second step changes on every push. Shipping the build makes the
# install a single command. Run `npm run build` and commit `lib/` with any
# source change; `test/bundle.test.ts` fails if the two drift or go missing.

# Runtime state this plugin and its producers create.
.dsh-progress/
*.log

# Editor and OS leftovers, so a contributor's tooling cannot end up in the
# published history.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local configuration and secrets: never committed, and never needed to build.
.npmrc
.env
.env.*

# Developer notes — plans, checklists, session handoffs — are local. They are
# written for one machine and one moment, they name local paths, and `docs/`
# ships inside the package while this must not: keeping them untracked is what
# stops a note from becoming a published artifact. Anything worth keeping for
# readers belongs in docs/, README.md, or the changelog.
notes/
